.TH CELLS 1 "" "cells 0.1.3" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cells \- a living microscope slide in your terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cells
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Animated immune cells, microbes, fungi, and bacteriophages. Sizes and
timings are illustrative. Requires Python 3.10 or later; interactive
mode requires curses on Linux or macOS (Windows users can use WSL).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
show this help message and exit
.TP
.B \-\-seed SEED
repeat a slide within the same program version (normally random)
.TP
.B \-\-scene SCENE
community preset
Choices: mixed, blood, microbial.
.TP
.B \-\-density 0.25..3
population multiplier
.TP
.B \-\-speed 0.125..8
simulation speed (normally 1; calm: 0.5)
.TP
.B \-\-fps 1..60
maximum frame rate (normally 30; calm: 10)
.TP
.B \-\-calm
slower motion, lower FPS, and no micropipette; explicit speed/fps win
.TP
.B \-\-style STYLE
presentation style; stained and raster are experimental
Choices: classic, stained, raster.
.TP
.B \-\-theme THEME
color palette; light suits white backgrounds
Choices: slide, amber, light, mono.
.TP
.B \-\-color COLOR
auto respects nonempty NO_COLOR; always overrides it
Choices: auto, always, never.
.TP
.B \-\-fill
tint cell bodies behind their glyphs (256\-color terminals)
.TP
.B \-\-unicode UNICODE
auto uses Unicode for UTF encodings
Choices: auto, always, never.
.TP
.B \-\-ascii
alias for \-\-unicode never
.TP
.B \-\-stats
show population and lifecycle statistics at startup
.TP
.B \-\-observe
caption lifecycle stages and recent events
.TP
.B \-\-no\-events
disable rare visitors and microscope events
.TP
.B \-\-screensaver
exit on any key
.TP
.B \-\-interactive
enable microscope tools; mouse or keyboard targeting
.TP
.B \-\-duration SECONDS
exit after this many wall\-clock seconds (normally unlimited)
.TP
.B \-\-snapshot
print one ASCII frame without terminal escapes and exit
.TP
.B \-\-size COLSxROWS
snapshot dimensions, up to 500x200
.TP
.B \-\-at SECONDS
simulation time for snapshot
.TP
.B \-\-diagnostics
print terminal capability information as JSON and exit
.TP
.B \-\-version
show program's version number and exit
.SH CONTROLS
q/Escape quits; Space pauses; +/\- changes speed; r resets the slide;
s toggles statistics; ? toggles help; j/k or arrows scroll help;
Ctrl-L redraws. Screensaver mode exits on any key except resize.
With interactive mode: 1 Inspect, 2 Lyse, 3 Feed, 4 Stir; left-click or
Enter applies. Arrows/hjkl aim; Tab selects and follows an entity.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
A nonempty value disables automatic color. Explicit \-\-color always overrides it.
.TP
.B TERM
Must identify the actual terminal for interactive mode.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
cells \-\-scene microbial \-\-calm
cells \-\-theme light \-\-observe
cells \-\-snapshot \-\-seed 42 \-\-size 100x32 \-\-at 30
.fi
.SH NOTES
Snapshots are ASCII without escape codes. Duration is wall time;
snapshot time is simulated time. A seed is reproducible within the
same version, size, and update/resize history. Normal quits, SIGINT,
and SIGTERM restore terminal settings. SIGKILL cannot run cleanup.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success; 1 on terminal failure; 2 for invalid usage or missing curses.
